The choice of $\tau_d = 0.1$ mm represents a conservative threshold: end-effector displacement below this value is physically negligible in manipulation tasks where typical action magnitudes are 1--10 mm per step. Our conclusions hold for any threshold in the range $[0.01, 1.0]$ mm.


